{"id":"chatcmpl-4324bd8e-e19f-4b23-a268-7064442bd110","object":"chat.completion","created":1795250384,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation where ambiguous spatial findings (laterality on a lateral view) are resolved by querying multiple independent expert models. The key insight is that lateral views complicate laterality determination, so redundant model consensus is used to increase confidence before committing to an answer. The pattern generalizes to any visual QA task where a single view is spatially ambiguous and multiple specialized tools can independently corroborate a finding.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When image metadata (e.g., view type, laterality markers) creates spatial ambiguity, explicitly surface that metadata in the tool query so models reason about the correct frame of reference.\",\n    \"Use two or more independent expert models to cross-validate a specific spatial or diagnostic claim, and only finalize the answer when they agree.\",\n    \"Decompose the question into a targeted sub-question (location/laterality) rather than asking the full multiple-choice question directly to each tool.\",\n    \"Match the tool to the modality: route imaging questions to imaging-specialist models rather than general-purpose QA models.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Always pass view/orientation metadata (e.g., 'lateral view', 'LT LAT') into tool queries; ask tools to localize findings anatomically before answering laterality.\",\n    \"Ambiguous spatial reasoning\": \"When a single perspective cannot disambiguate left vs right, query multiple models and require consensus before answering.\",\n    \"Multi-tool consensus\": \"Ask each tool a focused, differently-phrased version of the same sub-question to reduce correlated errors, then aggregate.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the image view/orientation metadata is included in every tool query before interpreting laterality.\",\n    \"Verify that at least two independent tools agree on the specific finding and location before selecting the final option.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":507,"total_tokens":904,"completion_tokens":397,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":507},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":397}}}